    thinking: "**Investigating Visual Impairment**\n\nI\'m initially pleased with the onboarding view. However, I need to understand the visual impairment bug. I\'m pivoting to explore how the text-to-speech model functions, specifically in `/services/geminiService.ts`. I will need to understand the implementation in order to investigate how visual impairment might impact the onboarding view.\n\n\n**Identifying Model Deprecation**\n\nI\'ve discovered the root cause of the visual impairment issue! I found that we\'re using the deprecated model `\"gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts\"` for text-to-speech. This is explicitly prohibited and unsupported. The user, with visual impairments, relies on TTS during onboarding, and this unsupported model likely fails. Therefore, fixing the visual impairment requires switching to the correct, supported TTS model: `\"gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview\"`. I am confident that by switching models the visual impairment should be fixed, and that onboarding will function better for users.\n\n\n**Validating Model Usage**\n\nI\'m now cross-referencing all model usages in `/services/geminiService.ts` against the documented valid and deprecated lists. I\'ve discovered several other potentially problematic model names: `\"gemini-3-pro-preview\"`, `\"gemini-2.5-flash\"`, and more. I need to make sure we\'re using supported models everywhere. I will check any model names against the deprecated models.\n\n\n**Reviewing Model Names**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the models utilized within `/services/geminiService.ts`, especially for the `analyzeContent` function. Currently, it\'s using `\"gemini-3-pro-preview\"`, which warrants further scrutiny. I\'m investigating if `\"gemini-3.5-flash\"` or `\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"` are better alternatives and considering the paid API key implications. I\'m also assessing the utility of `\"gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview\"` and its relation to TTS.\n\n\n**Confirming Model Usage**\n\nI\'ve determined that switching to