using `handlePlayAudio` and `decodePCM16` to fail too. I\'m verifying that the correct model, `\"gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview\"`, returns PCM16, as per the documentation, so that decoding into an `AudioBuffer` is valid. I\'m verifying the `decodePCM16` implementation for correctness.\n\n\n**Confirming Model Names**\n\nI\'m now certain the audio decoding process is valid, particularly the PCM16 format at 24000 sample rate, assuming `\"gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview\"` is used for TTS. I need to be more mindful of model names, and I have just realized that the model name for content analysis, `\"gemini-3-pro-preview\"`, is potentially an issue. I\'m verifying that model name against the deprecated list.\n\n\n**Optimizing Model Usage**\n\nI\'m now switching `gemini-3-pro-preview` to the faster `gemini-3.5-flash` in `/services/geminiService.ts` for analysis. I\'m updating `modelName` on line 55. I\'ve also identified an instance of `\"gemini-2.5-flash\"` at line 140. Although not strictly forbidden, I\'m replacing it with `\"gemini-3.5-flash\"` to maintain consistency and leverage its speed advantages. I\'ll need to confirm that `model` on line 208 is correct.\n\n\n**Prioritizing User Gestures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on audio autoplay constraints in the browser to ensure TTS works smoothly. I\'ve realized user interaction, like clicking a mode button, *should* satisfy gesture requirements, but some users have reported it doesn\'t. To improve accessibility and user experience, I\'m adding an explicit \"Tap Anywhere to Read Out\" overlay, verbal prompt, or onboarding step, to ensure audio playback is triggered. I\'m verifying the fix addresses the reported \"visual impairment issue\" with image uploads.\n\n\n"
