  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Successful Build**\n\nI\'m pleased to report a successful build! Everything compiles without errors, which is a great start. Now, I\'m shifting my focus to `/services/geminiService.ts` to conduct a thorough review. I\'m specifically aiming to identify any potential deprecated models or errors within the code. Currently, I\'m zooming in on line 55.\n\n\n**Evaluating Model Options**\n\nI\'ve been re-evaluating the model options, particularly for multimodal tasks. It seems that `\'gemini-3.5-flash\'` is the recommended model, which supports image, audio, and video inputs, and is also extremely fast. This is a very advantageous model! Currently, in our `geminiService.ts` code, the default `modelName` is still `\"gemini-3-pro-preview\"`. I am planning to replace this paid model with the faster, free, and recommended `\'gemini-3.5-flash\'` model, to avoid a paid key flow.\n\n\n**Refining Model Selection**\n\nI\'m now refining model selections based on task type. For basic text tasks, I\'ll default to `\'gemini-3.5-flash\'`. I\'ve confirmed it handles JSON schema output, which is a key requirement, by using `responseMimeType: \"application/json\"`. I\'ve also found an issue with the speech generation. The current model on line 208, `\"gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts\"`, is deprecated. I must replace it with `\'gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview\'`, as per the rules.\n\n\n**Updating Speech Generation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on speech generation. I\'ve found example code utilizing `\'gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview\'` within the `gemini-api/SKILL.md` file. I\'m noting the `responseModalities` requirement with a single `Modality.AUDIO` element, along with a `speechConfig` and `voiceConfig`. This is important, as my current `generateSpeech` function uses a deprecated model, `\'gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts\'`, on line 208 of `geminiService.ts`. I will replace this.\n\n\n**Refining Voice Configuration**\n\nI am now updating the `generateSpeech` function. I had to focus on the `contents` field format, which is `{ parts: [{ text: text }] }`, and the deprecated model name `\"gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts\"`. I am now using the correct model `\"gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview\"`. I am also evaluating voice options, and I will be passing the `voiceName` from the user or defaulting to a prebuilt voice like `\"Puck\"` or `\"Kore\"`, as listed in the skill! Both are beautiful, let\'s also evaluate the loading of other models such as the transcribeAudio function.\n\n\n**Addressing Deprecation Warnings**\n\nI\'ve just run into a deprecation warning with the `transcribeAudio` function! I noticed that I was using `\"gemini-2.5-flash\"`, which, upon further review, is indeed deprecated. I\'ll need to identify a supported model for audio transcription and adjust the code accordingly, as the current implementation is strictly prohibited. I\'m taking the opportunity to re-verify the list of deprecated models to ensure I haven\'t missed any other instances.\n\n\n**Optimizing Model Usage**\n\nI\'m now changing my model preferences again! I\'ve confirmed that `\'gemini-2.5-flash\'` is NOT deprecated, but I\'ve updated `transcribeAudio` to use `\'gemini-3.5-flash\'` because it handles multimodal input well, which is an amazing upgrade! I\'m also updating `sendChatMessage` to `\"gemini-3.5-flash\"`, which will improve the user experience with free, fast, and optimized chat responses! I will see how to address the visual impairment issue in the future.\n\n\n**Enhancing Accessibility Features**\n\nI\'m now focusing on improving accessibility. The autoplay feature in `ResultView` relies on `generateSpeech`, which I\'ve updated to use the correct model. This ensures immediate audio feedback for visually impaired users. I\'m exploring further enhancements for a hands-free experience. I will investigate how we can better support spatial descriptions.\n\n\n**Implementing Audio Feedback**\n\nI\'m now focusing on audio feedback for visually impaired users. I\'ve realized there\'s a critical silence during the image analysis stage. To address this, I\'m planning to implement audio cues for uploads. Initially, I\'ll leverage `window.speechSynthesis` for quick notifications like \"Image uploaded. Analyzing...\". If needed, I will generate a short audio notification as an alternative! I will verify the iFrame restrictions as per the guidelines.\n\n\n**Improving Accessibility Implementation**\n\nI\'m now implementing audio cues for visually impaired users during image analysis. The existing plan uses `window.speechSynthesis` or Web Audio. I\'m prioritizing `window.speechSynthesis` with fallback to HTML5 speech synthesis to notify users, especially those with visual impairments (`prefs.disability === UserDisability.VISUAL`). When the analysis begins, the system will speak \"Analyzing your image, please wait...\" This ensures the user is aware of the ongoing process. I\'ll evaluate the implementation of screen reader labels, keyboard tabIndex, high-contrast styling, etc.\n\n\n**Integrating Full Audio Summary**\n\nI\'m now integrating full audio summaries for improved accessibility. I\'ll automatically read the full description, encompassing the topic, spatial details, and tactile suggestions, for visually impaired users. I plan to add a unified playback control to easily play/pause the full spoken output, replacing the old auto-play function. I\'ll read `types.ts` again to verify all parameters are kept. I will check for other outdated models in `/services/geminiService.ts`.\n\n\n**Refining API Key Handling**\n\nI\'ve just focused on robust API key handling. I\'ve updated the `geminiService.ts` to use `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY || process.env.API_KEY`, ensuring flexibility and compliance. I am also planning to investigate thinking budget requirements to properly handle model calls, and to ensure we can meet all specifications. I am also reviewing the line 55 default model name.\n\n\n"
