  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing UX Improvements**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the build success! Now, I\'m diving into `App.tsx` with a focus on enhancing the user experience for visually impaired users. My initial focus is how they upload an image. The \"Hear Images\" button on the home screen triggers a specific function, which I\'m now examining in detail to identify potential improvements.\n\n\n**Adding Speech Feedback**\n\nI\'ve been examining the file upload flow closely. My current focus is how to improve the experience for users who require accessibility features. Specifically, I\'m exploring the potential to add speech feedback whenever the app enters the `ANALYZING` state. I\'m looking at how to trigger an announcement during this transition to better inform the user about the process.\n\n\n**Implementing Speech Alerts**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on integrating speech announcements within `App.tsx` during the `ANALYZING` state. My goal is to ensure that a visual impaired user knows image analysis has begun. I\'m considering using the WebSpeech API for an announcement or generate speech announcements. The `renderAnalyzing` function is the focal point, with a `useEffect` hook to prevent infinite loops. My current thinking is a simple announcement to inform that the app is in the processing phase.\n\n\n**Refining Announcement Logic**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the current approach! The verbal confirmation, \"Image uploaded successfully. I am now analyzing the image under Hear Images mode. Please wait...\" is exceptionally impactful. I\'m focusing on the language settings now. I\'m going to consult the constants in `constants.ts` to see what languages we can support: `SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES = [\"English\", \"Hindi\", \"Hinglish\", \"Tamil\", \"Telugu\", \"Kannada\", \"Bangla\", \"Assamese\", \"Marathi\", \"Odia\", \"Spanish\", \"French\"]`. I\'m going to look into support for customized voice overlay messages, too.\n\n\n**Expanding Language Support**\n\nI\'ve successfully implemented language support for speech announcements! I\'ve incorporated Hindi and Spanish translations into the announcement logic. I\'ve integrated language codes and tailored the verbal feedback to match the user\'s preferred language, offering a more inclusive experience. I\'m focusing on ensuring accurate and natural-sounding translations.\n\n\n**Adding More Languages**\n\nI\'ve been working on expanding language support further. I\'ve now integrated French, Tamil, and Telugu translations into the speech announcement system. I\'ve updated the logic to accommodate these new languages by defining text and language codes. The announcement adapts dynamically based on the user\'s selected language settings, improving inclusivity. I\'m focusing on ensuring each translation flows naturally in the announcement.\n\n\n**Adding More Languages**\n\nI\'ve been working on expanding language support even further, including Kannada, Bangla, and Assamese translations into the speech announcement system. I\'ve updated the logic to accommodate these new languages by defining text and language codes. The announcement adapts dynamically based on the user\'s selected language settings, improving inclusivity. I\'m focusing on ensuring each translation flows naturally in the announcement.\n\n\n**Adding Odia Support**\n\nI\'ve just added Odia translations to the speech announcement system! I\'ve updated the logic to accommodate Odia by defining the text and language code, and now the announcement adapts dynamically to the user\'s selected language setting, improving inclusivity further. I\'m focusing on ensuring this translation flows naturally in the announcement.\n\n\n**Designing Auto-Speech Features**\n\nI\'m now focusing on enhancing accessibility within `ResultView.tsx`. My goal is to automatically read out the result content for visually impaired users. I\'m considering a feature called \"Comprehensive Auto-Speech / Accessibility Companion.\" Instead of only reading the spatial description, I\'ll be creating a comprehensive summary that also includes the topic.\n\n\n**Improving Audio Interaction**\n\nI\'m now integrating replay and pause functionality for the auto-speech feature in `ResultView.tsx`. My focus is to allow users to interact with the audio, not just passively listen. I\'m exploring ways to connect the existing audio controls on the card to the full speech output. The aim is to give granular control over the audio, ensuring the user can pause, replay, and choose to listen to parts of the result at their convenience. I am thinking of enhancing the audio button to have this flexibility.\n\n\n**Refining Audio Control**\n\nI\'m now examining `HearImagesView()` and the `/components/ResultView.tsx` file for fine-tuning the auto-speech playback controls. I\'m focusing on lines 193-219, where I\'ll explore how to refine the audio button within the `Card` component for improved interaction. I want to ensure the audio controls offer a seamless user experience. I am examining whether a long press could trigger different functionality.\n\n\n**Adding Tactile Model Speech**\n\nI\'m now integrating a \"Listen to Tactile Idea\" button within `ResultView.tsx`. This addition enhances accessibility significantly, allowing users to effortlessly hear the tactile model suggestion. It mirrors the existing \"Listen\" button for the spatial description, promoting a consistent user experience. I\'m excited by this implementation for its quality-of-life improvements.\n\n\n**Integrating Tactile Model Playback**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated the \"Listen to Tactile Idea\" button within `ResultView.tsx`, enabling effortless playback of tactile model suggestions. It mirrors the existing \"Listen\" functionality, offering a cohesive experience. I\'m pleased with its quality of life improvement to give user autonomy.\n\n\n**Implementing Full Summary Playback**\n\nI\'m now implementing a \"Listen to Everything\" playbar. My thinking is to offer visually impaired users an immediate way to hear the entire visual guide, without requiring them to go through multiple small elements. I\'ve written a handle for the button and will render a full-width panel at the top of `ResultView` when the user has custom preferences for visual impairment. I am writing logic to ensure the content is comprehensive and includes topic, description and tactile suggestions.\n\n\n"
