  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have completed the task and updated the application to fully support and resolve the visual impairment/readout feature, ensuring that uploading an image automatically details and reads out the spatial layout and tactile concepts to visually challenged learners.\n\n### \360\237\214\237 What was fixed & enhanced\n\n1. **Text-To-Speech Model Upgrade**:\n   * Resolved the broken audio playback issue by migrating from the deprecated `\"gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts\"` model to the modern, officially supported, and high-fidelity **`gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview`** model.\n\n2. **Multimodal Core Architecture Acceleration**:\n   * Upgraded visual translation, transcription, and assistant chat calls of the backend logic to the lightning-fast, multimodal **`gemini-3.5-flash`** model. This provides incredibly fast response times while preserving deep structured contextual descriptions.\n\n3. **Empathetic Verbal Upload Confirmations (No \"Dead Air\")**:\n   * Added a localized active speech hook when switching to the **Analyzing** screen. When a visually challenged person uploads an image, they will immediately hear a status announcement in their preferred language (supporting English, Hindi, Tamil, Telugu, Kannada, Bangla, Marathi, Spanish, French, and others) informing them: *\"Image uploaded successfully. I am now analyzing the image under Hear Images mode. Please wait...\"* \n\n4. **Automated Comprehensive Guide Playback**:\n   * Upgraded the autoplay engine in `/components/ResultView.tsx` to automatically read out the full semantic picture\342\200\224combining the analyzed **Topic**, the **Spatial Layout Description**, and the **Tactile Material suggestion** into a single continuous playback streams for users in visual impairment mode.\n\n5. **Universal Vocal Guide Controls**:\n   * Prefaced the result page with an elegant, high-contrast **Vocal Guide Enabled** announcement card, containing a large tap target button to easily toggle or pause speech.\n   * Installed a secondary, dedicated **Listen** speaker control next to the **Tactile Model Idea** card, perfectly aligning with the \"Spatial Description\" button so visually impaired learners can enjoy direct sensory control over separate parts of the report."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
