    modified_response: "I have corrected the duplicate voice playback issues across the application, improving accessibility for visually impaired users:\n\n### Solutions Implemented \n\n* **Stopped Browser Speech Overlap (`App.tsx` & `ResultView.tsx`)**:\n  * Added a `React.useEffect` cleanup trigger to `App.tsx` which immediately invokes `window.speechSynthesis.cancel()` once processing completes (transitioning out of the `ANALYZING` state). This guarantees that the introductory *\"Analyzing image...\"* vocal cue from the browser instantly silences and does not overlap with the generated description.\n  * Added a master `window.speechSynthesis.cancel()` call at the top of the general playback function (`handlePlayAudio`) as defense-in-depth, halting any unexpected browser voice engines before Gemini\'s multimodal speaker output initiates.\n\n* **Guarded and Cleaned Up Autoplay (`ResultView.tsx`)**:\n  * Introduced a persistent state reference `autoPlayHasRunRef` to make sure the visual description for **Hear Images** mode starts exactly once per view, resolving double-triggering caused by React strict mode or rapid component updates.\n  * Extracted and stored the autoplay deferred timeout inside a local `timerId` handle to clear the timer block on view disassembly, preventing lingering timers from executing back-to-back duplicate voice streams on slow networks."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
